<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:45:13 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>What changes if Democrats win a majority in Congress?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-what-changes-if-democrats-win-a-majority-in-congress</link><description>
Americans head to the polls on Tuesday for the US midterm elections, which could flip the majority in one or both houses of Congress from the Republicans to the Democrats. What would a Democratic majority mean for the country's political landscape, and how might Democrats move to keep President Donald Trump in check?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce5e5364-d6d3-11f1-805b-730585255cda</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:29:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d61f8930-c86c-11f1-ab9a-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/main-pouvoir-congres-democrate.jpg">© France Médias Monde Graphics Studio</source><dc:creator>Romain HOUEIX</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nine dead in small plane crash near Trump's Florida home</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-nine-dead-in-small-plane-crash-near-trump-s-florida-home</link><description>
Nine people were killed Sunday when the Learjet they were travelling in plummeted into a neighbourhood in southern Florida, just miles from US President Donald Trump's resort home of Mar-a-Lago, officials said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1373b412-d6cf-11f1-99ce-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1373b412-d6cf-11f1-99ce-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/mini2-5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b016d92a-d6cf-11f1-9bcd-cb669b5f6870</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:33:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Heading into the midterms, 'no US president in recent times has been as unpopular as Donald Trump'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/heading-into-the-midterms-no-us-president-in-recent-times-has-been-as-unpopular-as-donald-trump</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics at Queen Mary University of London. He says that "Donald Trump is damaged goods at this point in his presidency." With this uncompromising assessment, Johnson takes us through the political forces shaping the 2026 US midterm elections. Far from assuming that Trump's formidable campaigning instincts can once again mobilize Republican voters, Johnson questions whether the president's political influence has become a liability for the very party he once transformed. He points to a potentially significant realignment within the American electorate. Economic grievances, rising living costs, trade disputes and disillusionment with the war in Iran appear, in Johnson's reading, to be weakening important elements of the coalition that sustained Trump's return to power. Particularly consequential is the possibility that Latino voters, agricultural communities and sections of the MAGA electorate may be reconsidering their political loyalties or withdrawing from electoral participation altogether.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdbaa30e-d6cf-11f1-ab72-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-150111-151452-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdbaa30e-d6cf-11f1-ab72-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-150111-151452-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3190430-d6cf-11f1-96bf-b1807fb543aa</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:25:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Will Gen Z enthusiasm help turn Michigan Senate blue?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-will-gen-z-enthusiasm-help-turn-michigan-senate-blue</link><description>
Michigan’s Senate seat is a must-win for the Democratic Party as it seeks to take control of the upper house of Congress. There’s a surge of energy behind progressive candidate Abdul El-Sayed, especially among younger voters. But can Gen Z's enthusiasm translate into votes and help Democrats win a critical Senate seat?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4434a4ec-d6cc-11f1-94f1-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-815f4d3f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4434a4ec-d6cc-11f1-94f1-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-815f4d3f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33801bc8-d6cb-11f1-b8df-272a86085fe5</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:03:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>US midterm elections: North Carolina farmers hit hard by inflation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261102-us-midterm-elections-north-carolina-farmers-hit-hard-by-inflation</link><description>
On the eve of the midterm elections, US President Donald Trump's unpopularity is impacting Republicans across the board. Many states with seats once considered Republican strongholds are now on shaky ground. One of them is North Carolina, a rural state where one in five jobs is tied to agriculture.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dfd6204-d6be-11f1-ade0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-cbd2a019.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dfd6204-d6be-11f1-ade0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-cbd2a019.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5fb826f6-d480-11f1-bc79-6b6f931b1085</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 13:13:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Fanny ALLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Michigan Democrat's endorsement of Republican ruffles critical Senate race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-michigan-democrat-s-endorsement-of-republican-ruffles-critical-senate-race-1</link><description>
A prominent Michigan Democrat endorsed Republican Mike Rogers on Sunday, giving President Donald Trump's Republicans an unexpected boost in a critical US Senate race two days before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a093d6fc-d6ba-11f1-a802-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-39.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a093d6fc-d6ba-11f1-a802-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-39.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ca59cab4-d6ba-11f1-a3e4-dbf4303496ab</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 12:41:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Michigan Democrat Haley Stevens defects from party</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-michigan-democrat-haley-stevens-defects-from-party</link><description>
Democrats sought on Monday, November 2, to contain a rift in Michigan's US Senate race after one of their own crossed party lines to endorse the Republican candidate, as both parties made final pitches before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d395c4e-d6b0-11f1-852b-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13352aed.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d395c4e-d6b0-11f1-852b-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-13352aed.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd64b10e-d6af-11f1-8a60-21c2ea0fa8d8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 11:52:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Could Senate candidate James Talarico turn Texas blue?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-us-midterms-could-senate-candidate-james-talarico-turn-texas-blue</link><description>
In Texas, a Democrat hopes to achieve a feat not seen in the state for 38 years: winning a seat in the US Senate. James Talarico, a young elected official who openly and proudly professes his Christian faith, is facing off against Ken Paxton, a controversial figure in the Republican Party. And his campaign is even winning over some of Donald Trump’s voters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c073ffe-d215-11f1-91ad-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299284061928.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c073ffe-d215-11f1-91ad-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299284061928.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb8f63d6-d6a3-11f1-a3af-f3f127eb3f08</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 10:30:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>In California, illegal border crossings plummet under Trump administration</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261102-in-california-illegal-border-crossings-plummet-under-trump-administration</link><description>
It was one of US President Donald Trump's major campaign promises in 2024: putting an end to illegal crossings along the southern US border. Today, official data shows that promise has been kept: arrests for illegal crossings have plummeted by more than 93 percent since the peak of arrests under then-US President Joe Biden.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7195d970-d69e-11f1-a828-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20d2068f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7195d970-d69e-11f1-a828-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20d2068f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46803528-d482-11f1-a402-1d37b28bd99c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 09:36:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Wassim CORNET</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Michigan Democrat stuns party to back Republican candidate in critical Senate race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-michigan-democrat-stuns-party-back-republican-candidate-critical-senate-race</link><description>
A high-profile Democratic defection shook Michigan's Senate race on the eve of US midterm elections as Representative Haley Stevens threw her support behind Republican Mike Rogers rather than backing the Democratic candidate, Abdul Al-Sayed, who beat her in the primary race. The move exposed divisions within the party as control of Congress hangs in the balance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/446637b6-d64d-11f1-b4b0-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-01T183814Z-1515927286-RC26FOANA85M-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MICHIGAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/446637b6-d64d-11f1-b4b0-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-01T183814Z-1515927286-RC26FOANA85M-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MICHIGAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7d261ea-d68f-11f1-a978-7961ef71f8ba</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 08:20:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/446637b6-d64d-11f1-b4b0-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-01T183814Z-1515927286-RC26FOANA85M-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MICHIGAN.jpg">© Rebecca Cook, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Michigan Democrat's endorsement of Republican ruffles critical Senate race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/michigan-democrat-s-endorsement-of-republican-ruffles-critical-senate-race</link><description>
A prominent Michigan Democrat endorsed Republican Mike Rogers on Sunday, giving President Donald Trump's Republicans an unexpected boost in a critical US Senate race two days before midterm elections that will decide control of Congress. FRANCE 24's Caroline Baum brings us more with this report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dff313c2-d691-11f1-9535-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-083520-083702-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dff313c2-d691-11f1-9535-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261102-083520-083702-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4f10e7e-d691-11f1-9dee-a7dee986aadb</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 07:55:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Midterms 2026: Georgians on the front lines of the people’s war against data centres</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-midterms-2026-georgians-front-lines-people-war-against-data-centres</link><description>
Artificial intelligence emerged as a major issue on the 2026 US midterm campaign trail, with opposition to data centres drawing supporters across partisan divides united over ecological worries, increased utility bills and business interests outweighing citizen concerns. Georgia, the top US market for data centre construction, has been on the front line of the struggle. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7792b7ee-d491-11f1-b147-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/main-93.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7792b7ee-d491-11f1-b147-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/main-93.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9763282e-d491-11f1-9e9b-cb1f2e7eecaf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 06:11:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7792b7ee-d491-11f1-b147-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/main-93.jpg">© Mike Stewart, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Halloween weekend shootings across US leave at least six dead, dozens wounded</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-halloween-weekend-shootings-across-us-leave-at-least-six-dead-dozens-wounded</link><description>
A spate of shootings in nightlife districts and near university campuses across the United States over Halloween weekend left at least six people dead and dozens wounded, with Dallas recording the highest toll. Police were investigating multiple incidents in several states, while some suspects remained at large.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c665287a-bb41-11f1-9424-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T094246Z-237616975-RC28SNAUGKNH-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c665287a-bb41-11f1-9424-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T094246Z-237616975-RC28SNAUGKNH-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">32cb14f4-d657-11f1-904b-b798d30cad20</guid><pubDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:49:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c665287a-bb41-11f1-9424-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T094246Z-237616975-RC28SNAUGKNH-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg">© Toby Shepheard, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Nine killed as business jet crashes into South Florida neighbourhood</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261101-nine-killed-as-business-jet-crashes-into-south-florida-neighbourhood</link><description>
A business jet plunged into a South Florida neighbourhood on Sunday, killing all nine people aboard and exploding into a fireball near homes and a busy road. The pilot had reported icing, precipitation and severe turbulence before the Learjet entered a steep dive, according to air traffic control recordings.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9e60d24-aa3e-11f1-8a9c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T210859Z-932383450-RC2WDNASZYYQ-RTRMADP-3-USA-CRASH-PLANE-MIAMI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9e60d24-aa3e-11f1-8a9c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T210859Z-932383450-RC2WDNASZYYQ-RTRMADP-3-USA-CRASH-PLANE-MIAMI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4623867a-d64e-11f1-8af9-cfcbd374c49b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 23:45:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9e60d24-aa3e-11f1-8a9c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-06T210859Z-932383450-RC2WDNASZYYQ-RTRMADP-3-USA-CRASH-PLANE-MIAMI.jpg">© Marco Bello, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA[Michigan 'betrayal’ & midterm manoeuvres]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261101-michigan-betrayal-mid-term-manouvres</link><description>
FRANCE 24's Gavin Lee assesses the last-minute campaign dramas and takes a US election overview on the "must-watch states" alongside Professor Donald Green, Professor of Political Science at Columbia University and co-author of the definitive book "Get Out the Vote", and foreign affairs analyst Laurie Dundon, who previously served in the US State Department during the Clinton administration.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0fdb1aa-d62a-11f1-b8cd-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-US-POLITIQUE-0-00-01-00.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0fdb1aa-d62a-11f1-b8cd-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-US-POLITIQUE-0-00-01-00.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">babdc8ce-d62b-11f1-8248-bfd479b0b5c6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 19:37:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Democrats face leftward surge</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-democrats-face-leftward-surge</link><description>
As Democrats seek to regain control of Congress, divisions within the party are emerging over its future direction. A new wave of progressive candidates is pushing to shift priorities further to the left, challenging corporate money in politics and calling for universal healthcare, climate action and an end to police violence. Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0883ea4c-d5fb-11f1-958f-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-131203-131443-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0883ea4c-d5fb-11f1-958f-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-131203-131443-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0dbb5180-d5fb-11f1-9377-b5cd4537e7c7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 13:56:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Affordability at heart of Michigan race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-affordability-at-heart-of-michigan-race</link><description>
For many voters, the cost of living is the single biggest issue. Our reporters Jessica Le Masurier and Sarah Andersen travelled to Michigan to meet voters, where, according to one NGO, around 40% of the population struggle to afford basic necessities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb94adfa-d5d4-11f1-b7e9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-090841-091053-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb94adfa-d5d4-11f1-b7e9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261101-090841-091053-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c0bf083e-d5d4-11f1-9a9a-317c774189c1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 09:39:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump vs MAGA: Why his movement is splitting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261031-trump-vs-maga-why-his-movement-is-splitting</link><description>
As the 2026 midterm elections approach, divisions within the MAGA camp are becoming increasingly visible. From the war in Iran and rising fuel prices to the Epstein files, several of Trump’s decisions are fuelling divisions among his most loyal supporters.
 
Once united by a shared vision of America, MAGA now brings together factions that increasingly disagree over foreign policy, the economy and what “America First” should actually mean. Yet Trump remains the central figure holding this political coalition together – and he is fighting to keep it that way.
 
Why are some of the president’s longtime allies distancing themselves from him? Can MAGA remain united despite these disagreements? And can Trump still mobilise his base ahead of the midterms?
 
🔍 Our journalist Stella Elgersma breaks down the divisions within the MAGA movement and Donald Trump’s strategy to rally his supporters, once again.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b3c170e-d515-11f1-8178-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/MAGA-Why-Trump-s-movement-is-fracturing.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b3c170e-d515-11f1-8178-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/MAGA-Why-Trump-s-movement-is-fracturing.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7b932522-d513-11f1-b4d8-cbfbf7926c2d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:11:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'Atmosphere of fear': Trump moves to curtail voting rights ahead of the midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-united-states-atmosphere-of-fear-trump-moves-to-curtail-voting-rights-ahead-of-the-midterms</link><description>
Americans vote on November 3 in midterm elections that could see Republicans lose control of Congress, endangering US President Donald Trump's legislative agenda. Under the US Constitution, elections are organized by the respective states – but that has not halted US President Donald Trump from trying to wield his influence ahead of the vote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60e1826-cefb-11f1-8e8e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296071599538.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60e1826-cefb-11f1-8e8e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296071599538.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ff20120-cef9-11f1-9def-d5b4f242dc3a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:40:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e60e1826-cefb-11f1-8e8e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26296071599538.jpg">© Alex Brandon, AP</source><dc:creator>Kal BERJIKIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro posts video, says he fled Brazil due to ‘persecution’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261031-flavio-bolsonaro-posts-video-says-he-fled-brazil-due-to-persecution</link><description>
